# Driver API flow — run AFTER customer Request Ride + Confirm Ride
# Easiest: use e2e-ride-flow.http (auto-chains ride_id + OTP from customer steps)
#
# Manual mode: copy ride_id and OTP from customer Confirm Ride response into:
#   @rideId / @rideOtp below
#
# Driver must be verified (is_driver_verified=true) or accept returns 403.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@driverEmail = sridharshini@yopmail.com
@driverPassword =sri@123456 
@rideId = 6a072c4ad1dd1cbc1ea301d1
@rideOtp = 9918
@dropOtp = 0000
### Driver Login
# @name driverLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/drivers/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{driverEmail}}",
  "password": "{{driverPassword}}"
}

### Incoming Rides (within ~10 km — use coords near pickup)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/drivers/rides/incoming?lat=12.976&lng=80.221
Authorization: Bearer {{driverLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### Accept Ride
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/drivers/rides/{{rideId}}/accept
Authorization: Bearer {{driverLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### Arrived
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/drivers/rides/{{rideId}}/arrived
Authorization: Bearer {{driverLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### Verify OTP (use OTP from confirm ride — same code after arrived; do NOT call /arrived again before this)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/drivers/rides/{{rideId}}/verify-otp
Authorization: Bearer {{driverLogin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "otp": {{rideOtp}}
}

### Picked Up
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/drivers/rides/{{rideId}}/picked-up
Authorization: Bearer {{driverLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### In Transit (required before drop on Docker backend)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/drivers/rides/{{rideId}}/in-transit
Authorization: Bearer {{driverLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### Dropped (generates new drop OTP — copy drop_otp from response, NOT pickup OTP)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/drivers/rides/{{rideId}}/dropped
Authorization: Bearer {{driverLogin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fare": 250,
  "lat": 12.971,
  "lng": 80.242,
  "actual_distance_km": 5.2,
  "duration_min": 12
}

### Verify Drop OTP (use drop_otp from dropped response / customer app)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/drivers/rides/{{rideId}}/verify-drop-otp
Authorization: Bearer {{driverLogin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "otp": {{dropOtp}}
}

### Cash received (cash rides)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/drivers/rides/{{rideId}}/cash-received
Authorization: Bearer {{driverLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### Complete ride (after payment success)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/drivers/rides/{{rideId}}/complete
Authorization: Bearer {{driverLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### Wallet
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/drivers/wallet
Authorization: Bearer {{driverLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### Earnings summary (today, IST tz_offset=330)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/drivers/earnings/summary?period=today&tz_offset=330
Authorization: Bearer {{driverLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### Earnings summary (this week)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/drivers/earnings/summary?period=week&tz_offset=330
Authorization: Bearer {{driverLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### Earnings cash
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/drivers/earnings/cash
Authorization: Bearer {{driverLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### Earnings total
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/drivers/earnings/total
Authorization: Bearer {{driverLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### Ride history
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/drivers/rides/history
Authorization: Bearer {{driverLogin.response.body.$.token}}
